## Scope and coverage

The eight ready lessons cover the completed Week1 readings and lecture concepts available on 4 October2026. The semester plan is partial because later teaching content is absent; a topic title in the SIS outline is orientation, not an executable lesson. Deadline/retention horizon is unknown (`null`). JEB103 is identified in the finished organization note; the established course folder remains unchanged.

| Capability/material | Finished note and exact locator | Objectives | Coverage and limits |
|---|---|---|---|
| Six classification dimensions; mixed mechanisms | [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Comparing_Economic_Systems.md#What is being classified?]] | O001 | ready |
| Nine performance criteria; tables, Lorenz and evidence | [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Comparing_Economic_Systems.md#Comparing performance: define the outcome first]] | O002 | ready; historical/conditional data |
| Institution types and hidden information | [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Institutions_and_Economic_Development.md#What institutions are]] | O003 | ready; simplified model arithmetic and limits |
| Specific investment/commitment | [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Institutions_and_Economic_Development.md#2. Hold-up: investment changes bargaining power]] | O004 | ready; stated outside-option assumptions |
| Cooperation/coordination and governance | [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Institutions_and_Economic_Development.md#4. Cooperation: individual incentives defeat a shared gain]] | O005 | ready; pure-action game checks only |
| Persistence and political feedback | [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Institutions_and_Economic_Development.md#Why imperfect institutions can persist]] | O006 | ready; diagrams qualitative |
| Colonial extraction, Virginia incentives and Nogales | [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Colonial_Institutions_and_Divergence.md#Spanish colonization: creating rules for extraction]] | O007 | ready; no controlled causal estimate |
| Political power/finance/entrepreneurship | [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Colonial_Institutions_and_Divergence.md#From political rules to invention, firms, and finance]] | O008 | ready; relative historical comparison |
| Course orientation and assessment | [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Comparative_Economics/Week_1/Course_Organization_and_Week_1_Scope.md#Assessment]] | orientation for all | readable orientation; no learner acquisition claim |
