**Course orientation:** the finished note reports four seminar summaries/critical evaluations in weeks3,6,9,12 (20% combined), midterm20%, final60%. Final format includes multiple choice, model/graph problems and brief essay, with understanding/creative thinking emphasized. The route therefore prepares explanations, payoff/accounting applications and critical historical arguments; it does not guarantee full exam coverage. Original work is required. The separate syllabus/Moodle were not supplied and fractional-score rounding is undefined; do not turn printed integer bands into a grading rule. October2 introduction/October9 institutions in the SIS context does not cancel previously assigned Week1 readings. No timetable or review schedule is created.

