## Execution and assessment contract

Every ready lesson contains identity/current tuple, observable component criteria, exact note anchors, required prerequisites with diagnostics/keys/repair, definitions/intermediate reasoning, worked and completion examples, two distinct immediate and two distinct delayed full-scope checks, narrow fresh corrections, allowed help/tools, and advancement/stop rules. Each I/D key covers every component elicited by its prompt. Every permitted acquisition route uses two different unexposed full-scope I/D forms; corrections, worked/support and prerequisites cannot replace that role. D variants used immediately after repair are recorded as immediate and require fresh future delayed items if the bank is exhausted. Delayed success is separate, closed-note and at least24 elapsed hours after last instruction/solution exposure. This is an operational guard, not a personalized retention finding. No due date is set.

Expository note examples and figures support explanations; prompts supply all assessment data and preserve arithmetic/units/sign/causal cautions. Teaching retrieves the index, one prepared block and its selected note sections. Unprepared alternative answers, ambiguous keys and exhausted fresh banks produce a plan issue; academic contradictions go to ingest.

